@article{ WOS:001725714700001,
Author = {Agarwal, Alpana and Ojha, Ravindra},
Title = {Implications of the growing AI technology on society and SDGs: insights
   from the analytic hierarchy process and SWARA},
Journal = {JOURNAL OF ADVANCES IN MANAGEMENT RESEARCH},
Year = {2026},
Month = {2026 MAR 30},
Abstract = {PurposeIt is important to understand the risks, challenges, and adverse
   effects on Sustainable development goals (SDGs) associated with the
   accelerated growth of AI. New green initiatives are also evolving to
   mitigate these challenges. Therefore, it is imperative to analyse the
   relationship dynamics between the risks involved, their mitigating
   initiatives, and the SDGs.Design/methodology/approachThis study employed
   an extensive literature review, discussions with experts, and an
   examination of causality loops in AI challenges to achieve the SDGs. The
   stepwise weight assessment ratio analysis (SWARA) was deployed to
   identify the key challenges, and the analytic hierarchy process
   (AHP)facilitated an understanding of the relationships between AI
   challenges and mitigating initiatives.FindingsThe final synthesised
   outcome from AHP has prioritized the seven challenges from accelerated
   AI growth. The top three challenges - human inequality and biases, the
   increased digital divide, and unsustainable energy consumption
   constitute 79\% of the impact of the challenges to the growing AI
   applications.Research limitations/implicationsThe prioritised factors
   identified will serve stakeholders in developing relevant policies,
   investing in the right areas, and facilitating where to focus in the
   sustainability journey. AHP results have prompted the need for an
   index-the SDG Achievement Index (SAI). The index is expected to find
   application in real business.Originality/valueThe application of the AHP
   methodology to analyse the hierarchy and priorities in AI challenges and
   green initiatives is the original contribution of this research study.
   The suggested measure, SAI, is a useful approach for quantifying and
   tracking the trends of the impact of Green AI initiatives on the SDGs.
   The current research study is topical, enriching the literature, and
   insightful to practitioners.},
